WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.820
- All right. We always like
to end on a high note so that,

00:00:02.820 --> 00:00:05.550
see what we did there 'cause
I'm a singer. We're clever.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:08.170
So here's (chuckles)
one social media story

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.003
you can't miss.

00:00:09.003 --> 00:00:10.236
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:10.236 --> 00:00:12.998
(upbeat music)

00:00:12.998 --> 00:00:14.130
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:16.180
Lots of musicians feed off the power

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.900
of playing for huge audiences.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.050
But a banjo player in Colorado

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:22.800
has discovered the power
of playing for just one.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:26.560
His admirer: a wild Fox, who
often trots over to listen

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.391
while the man picks and
strums his bluegrass stylings.

00:00:30.391 --> 00:00:33.391
(man playing banjo)

00:00:47.246 --> 00:00:49.350
- (exclaims) What!?

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:52.760
Like, this is crazy to me.
I have been in the wild,

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.150
and they run from you.

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.250
Foxes run from you,
they're like, "Oh human."

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:57.083
Like, you know what I'm saying?

00:00:57.083 --> 00:00:58.610
They run. That's crazy.

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:02.430
We have this mesmerizing banjo
player on the line right now.

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:05.110
What's up Andy?
(audience claps)

00:01:05.110 --> 00:01:06.200
- What's up Kelly?

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.170
- I mean, literally been,

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.840
I've been like in Alaska
in like remote of remote,

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.560
all places and foxes run,
you try and get a picture

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.370
of those guys they just run from you.

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:16.650
You are serenading one.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.480
I don't know how that happened.

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:21.210
It's crazy. So, and this
happened a few times now, right?

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:22.570
Not just once.

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:25.210
- This has. It's been really amazing.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.300
We're really lucky to
live on a couple acres

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.210
up in the Boulder foothills.

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:32.430
So there's a lot of space
for animals to roam around.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:35.560
And I'm usually on tour a lot
with my band Leftover Salmon,

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:39.090
but when the pandemic hit,
we were home all the time.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:40.300
And I just sit on the deck,

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.930
playing banjo every day and
one day the Fox wandered over

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:47.021
and we thought, "Wow, I think
he's really loving the music."

00:01:47.021 --> 00:01:48.230
(Kelly chuckles)

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:50.310
And then another day I
was on a rock in the yard

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.410
and he literally came
and sat right next to me

00:01:53.410 --> 00:01:55.590
and just stared at me while I played banjo

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:57.245
and it was the coolest thing.

00:01:57.245 --> 00:01:58.620
- [Kelly] It is amazing.
- [Andy] And when my wife

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.030
finally captured it on
phone and we posted it,

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:01.890
people loved it.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.220
And now we've put a few videos up.

00:02:04.220 --> 00:02:06.732
We actually named the little guy Foxy too.

00:02:06.732 --> 00:02:08.458
(both laugh)

00:02:08.458 --> 00:02:09.368
- That's awesome.

00:02:09.368 --> 00:02:10.659
- [Andy] He was like, "Boo."

00:02:10.659 --> 00:02:13.460
- Did you say that your band's
name is Leftover Salmon?

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.293
- That's right.

00:02:14.293 --> 00:02:16.730
- That's an amazing band name.

00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:18.827
You said that like so
flippantly and I was like,

00:02:18.827 --> 00:02:20.520
"No, we're going to talk about it."

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.010
That's an amazing band name.

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:24.740
Y'all gotta check out Leftover Salmon.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.689
Thank you so much, Andy. I'm
liking your posts right now.

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:28.530
- [Andy] Thank You.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:29.770
- All right. That's not all my man.

00:02:29.770 --> 00:02:32.450
Our season long partner,
Pilot pen: makers of friction,

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:35.180
the go-to erasable pen of
"The Kelly Clarkson Show"

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:38.160
want to celebrate those creating
fearlessly, just like you.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:39.930
So they're going to give
you a thousand dollars.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.730
How's that sound?
(audience claps)

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:42.563
- Amazing?

00:02:42.563 --> 00:02:44.360
(Kelly laughs)
- Oh my God.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.080
- I love you, Andy. (laughs)

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.020
This is awesome.

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:48.580
Thank you so much, Andy.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:50.153
Keep playing for the Foxes.

